ow grass"}],"gloss":"on the low grass"},{"surface":"அமர்ந்து","parts":[{"text":"அமர்ந்து","lemma":"அமர்ந்து","gloss":"having sat"}],"gloss":"having sat"},{"surface":"உண்டு","parts":[{"text":"உண்டு","lemma":"உண்டு","gloss":"having eaten"}],"gloss":"having eaten"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அழல்","parts":[{"text":"அழல்","lemma":"அழல்","gloss":"fire"}],"gloss":"fire"},{"surface":"வாய்","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"வாய்","gloss":"mouth"}],"gloss":"mouth"},{"surface":"புக்க","parts":[{"text":"புக்க","lemma":"புகு","gloss":"entered"}],"gloss":"entered"},{"surface":"பின்னும்","parts":[{"text":"பின்னும்","lemma":"பின்னும்","gloss":"even after"}],"gloss":"even after"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பலர்","parts":[{"text":"பலர்","lemma":"பலர்","gloss":"many"}],"gloss":"many"},{"surface":"வாய்த்து","parts":[{"text":"வாய்த்து","lemma":"வாய்த்து","gloss":"praising"}],"gloss":"praising"},{"surface":"இராஅர்","parts":[{"text":"இராஅர்","lemma":"இரு","gloss":"they will not remain"}],"gloss":"they will not remain"},{"surface":"பகுத்து","parts":[{"text":"பகுத்து","lemma":"பகு","gloss":"having shared"}],"gloss":"having shared"},{"surface":"உண்டோரே","parts":[{"text":"உண்டோரே","lemma":"உண்ணுதல்","gloss":"those who ate indeed"}],"gloss":"those who ate indeed"}]}],"literal":"Greatly not-satisfied small angry-ones / few with-words many of-learning-ones / subtle with-intellect great of-giving-ones / stirred with-juice cool of-clarified-wine-ones / ripe-fruit with-seasoning rich of-sauce-ones / humility rejoicing embracing of-words-ones / benefit to-cause to-many having-helped / protection to-be this-land those-who-ruled / are-few-indeed O-Great-One listen now always / are-many-indeed nature that those-who-do-not-know-indeed / such-people's wealth-also enduring will-not-stand / still like-that its nature therefore / always virtue you-did-not-fail gift / those-who-desire in-hand filling please-protect fearfully / vulture perching having wasteland O-Magadha / cactus grown cremation-ground on-the-side-of / memorial-stone erected afterwards toddy-and-cooked-food / on-the-grass placed few cooked-rice food / funeral-priest to-command on-the-low-grass having-sat-and-eaten / fire-mouth entered even-after / many-praising will-not-remain those-who-shared-and-ate-indeed","translation":"Those who were not easily satisfied but had little anger, who spoke few words but possessed vast learning, who had subtle intellect and gave great gifts, who drank cool clarified wine with stirred honey, who ate rich sauces seasoned with ripe fruits, who rejoiced in humility and spoke embracing words, and who ruled this land as a shield, helping many to find benefit—such rulers are few, O Great One! Listen, those who do not know this truth are always many. Even the wealth of such great ones does not endure; such is its nature. Therefore, do not fail in your daily virtue; protect the hands of those who desire gifts by filling them. O Magadha! In the wasteland where vultures perch, on the side of the cremation ground where cactus grows, after a memorial stone is erected, a funeral priest will offer a little cooked rice on the grass along with toddy. Even after entering the mouth of the fire, those who shared and ate their food will not fail to live on, praised by many.","modern":"பெரிய அளவில் திருப்தியடையாத, ஆனால் சிறிய கோபமே கொண்டவர்கள்; சில சொற்களைப் பேசிப் பல நூல்களைக் கற்றவர்கள்; நுட்பமான அறிவோடு கொடைத்தன்மை மிக்கவர்கள்; தெளிந்த குளிர்ந்த மதுவை அருந்துபவர்கள்; கனிந்த பழங்களின் தாளிப்புடன் கூடிய கொழுத்த துவையலை உண்பவர்கள்; பணிவை விரும்பித் தழுவும் சொற்களைப் பேசுபவர்கள்; பலருக்கும் நன்மைகளைச் செய்து இந்நிலத்தைக் காவல் அரணாக நின்று ஆண்டவர்கள் மிகச் சிலரே, பெருமானே! கேட்பாயாக! இந்நிலையின் இயல்பை அறியாதவர்கள் எப்போதும் பலரே ஆவர். அத்தகையோரின் செல்வமும் நிலைத்து நிற்பதில்லை; அதுவே செல்வத்தின் இயல்பு. அதனால், நாள்தோறும் உனது அறநெறியைத் தவறாமல் கடைப்பிடிப்பாயாக; உன்னிடம் இரப்பவர்களின் கைகளை நிரப்பிக் காப்பாயாக. அச்சம் தரும் பருந்துகள் தங்கும் சுடுகாட்டின் கள்ளிச் செடிகள் நிறைந்த பகுதியில், நடுகல் நடப்பட்ட பிறகு, புலையன் ஏவ, புல்லின் மேல் அமர்ந்து, கள்ளோடு படைக்கப்பட்ட சில சோற்றுத் திரளையை உண்டு, நெருப்பில் வெந்து மடிந்த பின்னரும், பிறரோடு பகிர்ந்து உண்டவர்கள் மட்டுமே பலருடைய போற்றுதலில் என்றும் நிலைத்து வாழ்வார்கள்.","explanation":"The poet Caṅka Varuṇar addresses a king (referred to as Magadha) on the transience of life and wealth, urging him to practice charity. He describes the qualities of great rulers of the past who were wise, generous, and humble, noting that such noble kings are rare while ignorant ones are many. He emphasizes that wealth does not last, and after death, one is reduced to a simple offering of rice and toddy on the grass by a memorial stone in a desolate cremation ground. The transition from the luxurious life of kings (drinking clarified wine, eating rich seasoned sauces) to the stark, terrifying imagery of the cremation ground (vultures, cactus, a simple offering of rice on the grass) highlights the theme of impermanence (Kāñci tiṇai). The key words are 'பகுத்துண்டோரே' (those who shared and ate), which highlights the ultimate virtue that survives death, and 'மன்னி நில்லாது' (does not endure), pointing to the transience of wealth.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.89],[1.0,1.3],[1.3,1.5],[1.5,2.3],[2.3,2.63],[2.63,2.8],[2.8,3.0],[3.0,3.58],[3.58,4.44],[4.44,4.87],[4.87,5.77],[5.77,5.9],[6.03,6.7],[6.7,7.0],[7.0,7.24],[7.24,7.62],[7.62,8.39],[8.39,8.97],[9.24,9.5],[9.5,9.97],[9.97,10.56],[10.56,11.01],[11.3,11.6],[11.6,12.8],[12.8,13.26],[13.26,13.7],[13.7,14.1],[14.1,14.9],[14.9,15.1],[15.1,16.09],[16.09,16.88],[16.88,17.48],[17.48,17.81],[17.88,18.08],[18.08,18.38],[18.38,18.68],[18.68,19.38],[19.38,19.56],[19.56,19.92],[19.92,20.28],[20.28,20.71],[20.71,21.58],[21.58,22.18],[22.18,22.48],[22.54,22.88],[22.88,23.38],[23.46,23.78],[23.78,24.08],[24.08,24.48],[24.48,24.88],[24.88,25.98],[25.98,26.48],[26.48,26.88],[26.88,27.28],[27.28,27.78],[27.78,28.08],[28.08,28.58],[28.58,29.08],[29.08,30.28],[30.28,